                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f5c8a34a-d8ce-4b4d-9de3-d1995c039d75",
                        "entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "feminine",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "детермини́рована"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4b9ce045-655c-43f5-9134-92cc33ca96a5",
                        "entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "детермини́рованы"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d0c4c47-1e73-36e8-834a-1d273cc4fb46",
                        "entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "glosses": [
                            "филос. страд. прич. прош. вр. от детерминировать; чем-либо обусловленный, предопределённый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "participle"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48156ea6-04c6-40cf-88af-d0bdc8cf7205",
                                "sense_id": "5d0c4c47-1e73-36e8-834a-1d273cc4fb46",
                                "text": "С точки зрения детерминизма свобода есть «ничто», она выходит из детерминированного ряда, она ничем не обусловлена, рожденное из неё не вытекает из предшествующих причин, из «чего-то»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bebd5548-3829-4b50-8338-ad63ac190977",
                                "sense_id": "5d0c4c47-1e73-36e8-834a-1d273cc4fb46",
                                "text": "Вера в детерминированную судьбу может привести к тому, что личность снимет с себя ответственность."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "95590a72-6e60-38fd-8c96-d5b2067156b7",
                        "entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "glosses": [
                            "адъектив., научн. заранее известный, определённый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "70a4549c-aaa8-4bd8-be33-05712d9078ff",
                                "sense_id": "95590a72-6e60-38fd-8c96-d5b2067156b7",
                                "text": "Характеристика деятельности головного мозга как рефлекторной означает у И. М. Сеченова прежде всего то, что это деятельность закономерная, детерминированная."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "670fb0b9-c3b5-4fdc-9145-37781ef15b37",
                                "sense_id": "95590a72-6e60-38fd-8c96-d5b2067156b7",
                                "text": "То, что выпадает в этот раз, никак не связано с предысторией. Здесь нельзя говорить о детерминированном прогнозе и можно иметь дело лишь со статистическими характеристиками — средними значениями, дисперсиями, распределениями вероятностей."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4bc83ed8-0ae5-45f3-bef4-cb9208867af8",
                        "source_entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "target_lang_word": "deterministic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "deterministic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3a27b98-6da4-3821-aa56-4cabdb36f477",
                                        "entry_id": "4dd0cf8a-7d62-3409-86d6-25ee2ead72a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, or relating to determinism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c4cb4d1-02c8-31ea-bac5-4633409d0791",
                                        "entry_id": "4dd0cf8a-7d62-3409-86d6-25ee2ead72a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having at most one instruction associated with any given internal state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a Turing machine"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdcf0269-5cf7-43d2-ad1e-2c2d31bdf5b2",
                                                "sense_id": "9c4cb4d1-02c8-31ea-bac5-4633409d0791",
                                                "text": "Another class, P, is a subset of NP, and includes all decision problems that can be solved by a (deterministic) Turing machine in polynomial time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2b71ceb-2508-3de1-8cd3-a8d2ff202272",
                                        "entry_id": "4dd0cf8a-7d62-3409-86d6-25ee2ead72a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having exactly predictable time evolution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a system"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f1b6834-c29a-3caa-b300-17a3f7c6bbcc",
                                        "entry_id": "4dd0cf8a-7d62-3409-86d6-25ee2ead72a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For a given particular input, always producing the same output through the same sequence of states."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of an algorithm"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e30a140-b67b-417d-9ce1-409919fc3259",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1b6834-c29a-3caa-b300-17a3f7c6bbcc",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, if the genetic algorithm has many advantages, their computation cost is higher as compared with deterministic algorithms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a8355225-d664-4d42-afd0-db21b3c83a9d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e85b1c6e-59be-35f3-9767-8c44707c8a52",
                        "target_lang_word": "determinate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "determinate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bbe5104-ffef-3f1a-8df2-828463e80e32",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Distinct, clearly defined."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dde8d56-a98a-41c5-b0b3-c420726d8425",
                                                "sense_id": "5bbe5104-ffef-3f1a-8df2-828463e80e32",
                                                "text": "Quantity of words and a determinate number of feet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd137f96-184b-415e-9e2d-38ab33e01b06",
                                                "sense_id": "5bbe5104-ffef-3f1a-8df2-828463e80e32",
                                                "text": "[…] on account of his responsibility to Norman and Marigold, and on account of his now determinate age, he considered himself ineligible for more dangerous service."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9899b3e-347e-3d39-9c52-a04ac72e65eb",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fixed, determined, set, unvarying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b06d8115-3eca-4016-8646-4b72a5d9ddc6",
                                                "sense_id": "d9899b3e-347e-3d39-9c52-a04ac72e65eb",
                                                "text": "[…] hym have ye taken by the hondes of vnrightewes perſones / after he was delivered by the determinat counſell and fore knoweledge of God / and have crucified and ſlayne hym / […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "945841d6-d9a1-428c-a330-291ebb485566",
                                                "sense_id": "d9899b3e-347e-3d39-9c52-a04ac72e65eb",
                                                "text": "[S]he watched impatiently for the dawn of day, with that determinate purpoſe which generally inſures ſucceſs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1da2e2fe-fa16-3c7d-ade1-9d41f50ed308",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of growth: ending once a genetically predetermined structure has formed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c4cd9ac-4699-3163-aadd-719479752ba1",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conclusive; decisive; positive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28a85952-0d38-3887-8894-2c76f15ce684",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Determined or resolved upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4fe0e18-b6d4-448e-8812-420fa4eeed7c",
                                                "sense_id": "28a85952-0d38-3887-8894-2c76f15ce684",
                                                "text": "My determinate voyage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3bb5696-13da-4e84-9d92-2c4cd5d4b85f",
                                                "sense_id": "28a85952-0d38-3887-8894-2c76f15ce684",
                                                "text": "Francesca saw the danger of allowing this apathy to increase, and would fain have laid down some determinate scheme, and sought some fixed home and employment, which must have brought its occupations, its habits, and, finally, its interests."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c40d2c5-e0d9-3772-8277-0efe323589ac",
                                        "entry_id": "fe228bd8-b269-3e56-929c-ee1b50090263",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of determined purpose; resolute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65d44678-13fb-4489-a77c-3b982e87f583",
                                                "sense_id": "8c40d2c5-e0d9-3772-8277-0efe323589ac",
                                                "text": "More determinate to do than skilfull how to do.",
                                                "translation": "The New Arcadia",
                                                "english": "The New Arcadia"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
